+# Upwork Proposal Draft — $10k Procedural Industrial Homepage Loop
+
+**Status:** READY FOR HUMAN PASTE  
+**Listing:** https://www.upwork.com/freelance-jobs/apply/artist-animate-and-build-the-the-loop-animation-the-company-homepage_~022096976272432704858/  
+**Local proof:** `tools/fromage-webgl-kit/prototypes/procedural-industrial-loop/`  
+**Capture mode:** append `?capture=1` for chrome-free hero recording
+
+Do **not** auto-send. Paste only after you attach the stills / short loop preview.
+
+---
+
+## Cover letter (paste)
+
+Hi — I built a small clean-room mechanical proof specifically around the motion law in your brief, without reconstructing your CAD, brand, or proprietary scene.
+
+What the proof demonstrates:
+
+- absolute-time procedural choreography (pose is a pure function of timeline time)
+- piecewise-linear motion only — constant speed, hard stops, no easing / bounce / settle
+- one primary axis active per segment, then a mirrored return for a seamless 16s loop
+- monochrome machined base presentation, with color reserved for illustrative STRUCTURAL / FLOW / THERMAL visualization states
+- named hierarchy suitable for staged approval (geometry → materials → full assembly)
+
+Runtime-checked on desktop and phone-width; diagnostics are exposed in the demo.
+
+Production approach if shortlisted:
+
+1. import / clean your supplied CAD while preserving object naming  
+2. validate scale, normals, topology, material groups  
+3. drive transforms with the same deterministic absolute-time controller (no Bezier easing)  
+4. stage approvals: geometry/outliner → single-station light-on-light lookdev → full population  
+5. render the 16s master, then encode AV1/VP9 against the actual &lt;5 MB web-quality threshold  
+
+Questions I would confirm before locking the schedule:
+
+- preferred DCC for CAD cleanup (Blender or Houdini on my side)  
+- whether the supplied prototype’s timing table is authoritative, or we should match your written motion law exactly  
+- required delivery package for the source scene + staged stills  
+
+Happy to walk through the monochrome loop and visualization modes live.
+
+---
+
+## Attachments to include
+
+1. `evidence/capture_hero.png` — monochrome BASE hero  
+2. `evidence/mode_structural.png` / `mode_flow.png` / `mode_thermal.png` — color-for-information modes  
+3. `evidence/loop_preview.mp4` — short motion sample (re-record a full 16s locally if you want a cleaner clip)  
+4. Optional: `evidence/seed_01.png`–`seed_03.png` to show seeded variation  
+
+## Honest claim boundary
+
+Say: system thinking + motion-law obedience + staged production path.  
+Do **not** say: already rebuilt their CAD, already delivered ProRes/AV1 masters, or already integrated their proprietary prototype.
